{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01QnmR9BunKjhxQMt8sekqU8","type":"tool_result","content":"{\"result\":\"{\\\"success\\\": true, \\\"data\\\": {\\\"path\\\": \\\"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_9/projects/event-gated-adaptive-horizon/memory.md\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"# Memory\\\\n\\\\n## 2026-05-15: D035 — C6 Seed 计数修正\\\\n\\\\n**严重错误**：exp_008e_v3_subsample_on_dt1_h15（\\\\\\\"s0\\\\\\\"）和 exp_008e_v3_walker_s1（\\\\\\\"s1\\\\\\\"）命令行均为 `--seed 1`。eval=869.88 vs 869.9 的 \\\\\\\"nearly identical\\\\\\\" 是**确定性复现，不是跨 seed 一致性**。\\\\n\\\\n**结论**：C6 目前只有 **1 个独立 seed**（seed=1）。008e_v3_s2（seed=2, RUNNING）是第一个真正独立的 seed 验证，其结果对 C6 multi-seed claim 至关重要。\\\\n\\\\n**教训**：提交多 seed 实验前必须核验 `--seed` 参数不同于已有 runs。不要从 eval 数值 \\\\\\\"nearly identical\\\\\\\" 推断跨 seed 一致性——先排除确定性复现。\\\\n\\\\n## 2026-05-14: 文献增量扫描 — Novelty 安全，TAWM 强化贡献\\\\n\\\\n**literature_map.yaml**: 64 → 72 篇。\\\\n\\\\n**核心结论：无论文诊断过 dt_embedding → delusional critic → stochastic collapse 机制。Novelty 安全。**\\\\n\\\\n**TAWM (Nhu et al., ICML 2025)** 是最相关竞品——显式 Δt conditioning world model，但在 MPC 范式下。**反而强化我们的贡献**：TAWM 证明 Δt conditioning 在 MPC 中有效，我们发现它在 imagination-based actor-critic 中导致病态 value overestimation。\\\\n\\\\n**必须引用**：nhu2025tawm（区分 MPC vs imagination 范式）。**应当引用**：li2025lsimagine, shaj2023mts3。**考虑引用**：zhang2026hwm。\\\\n\\\\n**\\\\\\\"Delusional\\\\\\\" 术语追溯**：Lu & Schuurmans (NeurIPS 2018) 指 function approximation 下 Q-backup 的 policy inconsistency。我们的用法是该概念在 model-based imagination 中的新实例化，需在论文中明确引用和区分。\\\\n\\\\n## 2026-05-14: D032 — Collapse is Stochastic, nve>1.5x is Reliable\\\\n\\\\n**发现**：009b (008d seed 2) 未复现 delusional critic collapse。\\\\n\\\\n- 008d seed 1: nve **持续** >1.5x（1.78x→1.71x→2.09x→4.12x, 4 个连续 checkpoint） → collapse\\\\n- 009b seed 2: nve **瞬时** >1.5x（2.05x@25K 单点），回落至 0.38x@105K → no collapse\\\\n\\\\n**关键结论**：nve>1.5x 作为 trained dt_emb marker 100% reliable（4/4）；collapse 是 stochastic（1/2）。\\\\n\\\\n## 2026-05-14: 009c 教训 — dt_emb removal 的双重效应\\\\n\\\\n去掉 dt_embedding 有两个独立效应：(1) 消除 delusional critic ✓，(2) 严重退化 reward prediction ✗（MAE 75x baseline）。008f 实用含义降为\\\\\\\"消除 delusional critic 但引入 reward 噪声\\\\\\\"。C6 (008e_v3) 是唯一同时避免崩塌 + 保持 reward prediction + 达 95% baseline 的方案。\\\\n\\\\n## 2026-05-14: Actor Entropy 分析决策（Director 修正）\\\\n\\\\n**C2 cleanest comparison pair**: 008f vs 008d（仅 dt_embed_dim 不同）。措辞用 \\\\\\\"entropy convergence delayed\\\\\\\"。\\\\n\\\\n## 2026-05-14: Value Calibration — 最强诊断信号\\\\n\\\\nv/R ratio（eval_return 基准）完美分离 collapsed vs healthy。Collapsed: 008d peak v/R=1.67@55K, 006 peak v/R=2.72@65K。Healthy: 从未超过 1.0。判定阈值 v/R > 1.5 在 late training 100% 区分。Normalized v/e target 不具区分力（全部收敛至 ~1.0）。\\\\n\\\\n## 2026-05-14: D033 — 008e_v3 dt_embedding 实际是 trained\\\\n\\\\n代码审计确认：nn.Embedding 默认 trainable 且代码无 freeze/detach。**Critical variable 是 imagination dt，不是 embedding 训练状态。** C6 从\\\\\\\"改模型\\\\\\\"升级为\\\\\\\"改策略\\\\\\\"——实践者零成本采用。\\\\n\\\\n## 2026-05-14: 监控教训 — tail_training_logs 有 buffering 延迟\\\\n\\\\n监控训练进度应直接读 logdir/metrics.jsonl（通过 SSH read_only），不要依赖 tmux log。\\\\n\\\\n## 2026-05-14: Cheetah Run / Cartpole Swingup 环境验证\\\\n\\\\n代码无需修改，`--task dmc_cheetah_run` / `--task dmc_cartpole_swingup` 直接可用。Dry-run 4 配置全 PASS。Cartpole obs 5D + act 1D 远小于 Walker/Cheetah。\\\\n\\\\n## 2026-05-14: GPU 隔离确认\\\\n\\\\nCUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES 隔离正确。`--device cuda:0` + `CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=1` = 物理 GPU 1。监控 Worker 的 \\\\\\\"设备冲突\\\\\\\" 报告为误报。\\\\n\\\", \\\"total_chars\\\": 2750, \\\"truncated\\\": false}, \\\"error\\\": null, \\\"metadata\\\": {}}\"}"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01L4jssAZWLAQJYMSAJSFtZm","session_id":"31787645-5970-4613-84a7-699e9017e33d","uuid":"19ab926c-3390-4131-a706-1ff8488bac75","timestamp":"2026-05-15T01:50:41.439Z"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_011LB37Y11BcRhhPs7GpDGP3","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01ThN6WpRhxnFZ4u1h4UFPY2","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"R2: Novelty + Related Work review","prompt":"You are Reviewer R2 for a top ML venue review (acceptance rate ~25%, 6-point scale: 1=Strong Reject, 2=Reject, 3=Weak Reject, 4=Weak Accept, 5=Accept, 6=Strong Accept).\n\nYour focus: **Novelty and Related Work**.\n\n## Paper: \"Why Temporal Abstraction Fails in DreamerV3: A Diagnostic Analysis of Variable-Rate Imagination\"\n\n### Paper Summary\nThe paper diagnoses why variable-rate imagination fails in DreamerV3. The central claim is a closed causal chain: trained duration embeddings (dt_emb) exploit the RSSM's fidelity gap at dt>1, producing systematic value overestimation (\"delusional critic\"). They introduce \"normalized value-eval ratio\" (nve) as a diagnostic marker, achieving 18/18=100% classification accuracy across Walker Walk, Cheetah Run, and Cartpole Swingup (3 seeds each). A \"C6\" mitigation (restrict imagination to dt=1 while retaining multi-dt training) recovers 94.8% baseline in Walker Walk (3-seed IQM=870, CI [852,888]). An uncertainty-gated truncation pilot achieves 89% baseline.\n\n### Contributions Claimed\n1. Mechanism identification: closed causal chain from dt_emb → RSSM fidelity gap → value overestimation → actor collapse\n2. Quantitative diagnostic marker: nve>1.5× at 35K+ steps, 18/18=100% classification\n3. Cross-environment validation: mechanism replicates in Cheetah Run, Cartpole Swingup (+ Hopper Hop supplementary)\n4. Zero-cost mitigation: C6 (dt=1 imagination) recovers 94.8% baseline\n\n### Related Work as Presented\nThe paper covers three areas (Section 2, ~half a page):\n- **Temporal abstraction in RL**: Options framework (Sutton et al. 1999, Precup 2000), option-critic (Bacon et al. 2017), action-repeat (Lakshminarayanan et al. 2017, Sharma et al. 2017), FiGAR (Braylan et al. 2015)\n- **World-model RL**: Dreamer family (Hafner et al. 2019, 2020, 2021, 2023), RSSM\n- **Value overestimation in MBRL**: Model exploitation (Janner et al. 2019, Pan et al. 2020), non-delusional Q-learning (Lu et al. 2018)\n\nTotal references: ~14 (including Agarwal et al. 2021 for IQM, Henderson et al. 2018, Nikishin et al. 2022)\n\n### Key Technical Details\n- nve(t) = v/e_exp(t) / v/e_baseline(t), threshold 1.5× at steps ≥ 35K\n- RSSM fidelity gap: obs MSE ratio and reward MAE ratio between dt=1 and dt=2\n- dt_embedding: learned embedding vector conditioned on dt∈{1,2}, concatenated to RSSM state\n- C6: imagination restricted to dt=1, but training data still includes dt=2 transitions\n- Uncertainty-gated truncation: monitors RSSM prediction uncertainty, truncates dt>1 when uncertainty exceeds threshold (1-seed pilot only)\n- Environments: Walker Walk, Cheetah Run, Cartpole Swingup, Hopper Hop (all DMC)\n- 3 seeds per configuration, IQM with 95% CI following Agarwal et al. 2021\n\n### Full Experiment Coverage\nTables 1-14 cover baselines, RSSM fidelity, embedding analysis, trained/untrained/removed dt_emb across 4 environments, C6 mitigation, KL divergence analysis, actor entropy dynamics, uncertainty-gated pilot, and aggregate metrics.\n\n### Your Review Task\n\nEvaluate the following aspects thoroughly:\n\n1. **Novelty Assessment**\n   - Is identifying this failure mode genuinely novel? Value overestimation in MBRL is well-known (Janner 2019, Pan 2020). How much does this add?\n   - Is the nve diagnostic metric a meaningful methodological contribution?\n   - Is the C6 mitigation (\"just use dt=1 imagination\") trivially obvious in hindsight?\n   - Does \"diagnosing why something fails\" constitute a sufficient contribution for a top venue?\n\n2. **Related Work Completeness**\n   - Missing references? Consider: TD-MPC (Hansen et al. 2022), IRIS (Micheli et al. 2023), other Transformer-based world models, TWM, STORM, etc.\n   - Multi-step prediction error analysis in dynamics models — any prior work?\n   - Value overestimation diagnostics — any existing metrics similar to nve?\n   - Temporal difference learning at multiple scales — relevant work?\n\n3. **Positioning and Framing**\n   - Is this positioned correctly as a \"diagnostic analysis\" paper?\n   - Would it be better as a workshop paper or short paper?\n   - Does the scope (DreamerV3 only, DMC only) match the claims?\n   - The \"delusional critic\" terminology — appropriate use given Lu et al. 2018's \"non-delusional Q-learning\"?\n\n4. **Breadth of Impact**\n   - Who would benefit from reading this paper?\n   - Does it advance the field or just explain a negative result?\n   - How actionable are the findings beyond DreamerV3?\n\nProvide your independent assessment:\n- Summary of strengths (bullet points)\n- Summary of weaknesses (bullet points)\n- Questions for authors\n- Preliminary score (1-6) with confidence (1-5)\n- Short justification\n\nKeep your review under 800 words."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3,"cache_creation_input_tokens":36525,"cache_read_input_tokens":22969,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":36525},"output_tokens":16,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"31787645-5970-4613-84a7-699e9017e33d","uuid":"9ab08157-ef5e-491a-9783-ccd5c3a481f5"}
{"type":"system","subtype":"task_started","task_id":"a0b3db860deeec91c","tool_use_id":"toolu_01ThN6WpRhxnFZ4u1h4UFPY2","description":"R2: Novelty + Related Work review","task_type":"local_agent","prompt":"You are Reviewer R2 for a top ML venue review (acceptance rate ~25%, 6-point scale: 1=Strong Reject, 2=Reject, 3=Weak Reject, 4=Weak Accept, 5=Accept, 6=Strong Accept).\n\nYour focus: **Novelty and Related Work**.\n\n## Paper: \"Why Temporal Abstraction Fails in DreamerV3: A Diagnostic Analysis of Variable-Rate Imagination\"\n\n### Paper Summary\nThe paper diagnoses why variable-rate imagination fails in DreamerV3. The central claim is a closed causal chain: trained duration embeddings (dt_emb) exploit the RSSM's fidelity gap at dt>1, producing systematic value overestimation (\"delusional critic\"). They introduce \"normalized value-eval ratio\" (nve) as a diagnostic marker, achieving 18/18=100% classification accuracy across Walker Walk, Cheetah Run, and Cartpole Swingup (3 seeds each). A \"C6\" mitigation (restrict imagination to dt=1 while retaining multi-dt training) recovers 94.8% baseline in Walker Walk (3-seed IQM=870, CI [852,888]). An uncertainty-gated truncation pilot achieves 89% baseline.\n\n### Contributions Claimed\n1. Mechanism identification: closed causal chain from dt_emb → RSSM fidelity gap → value overestimation → actor collapse\n2. Quantitative diagnostic marker: nve>1.5× at 35K+ steps, 18/18=100% classification\n3. Cross-environment validation: mechanism replicates in Cheetah Run, Cartpole Swingup (+ Hopper Hop supplementary)\n4. Zero-cost mitigation: C6 (dt=1 imagination) recovers 94.8% baseline\n\n### Related Work as Presented\nThe paper covers three areas (Section 2, ~half a page):\n- **Temporal abstraction in RL**: Options framework (Sutton et al. 1999, Precup 2000), option-critic (Bacon et al. 2017), action-repeat (Lakshminarayanan et al. 2017, Sharma et al. 2017), FiGAR (Braylan et al. 2015)\n- **World-model RL**: Dreamer family (Hafner et al. 2019, 2020, 2021, 2023), RSSM\n- **Value overestimation in MBRL**: Model exploitation (Janner et al. 2019, Pan et al. 2020), non-delusional Q-learning (Lu et al. 2018)\n\nTotal references: ~14 (including Agarwal et al. 2021 for IQM, Henderson et al. 2018, Nikishin et al. 2022)\n\n### Key Technical Details\n- nve(t) = v/e_exp(t) / v/e_baseline(t), threshold 1.5× at steps ≥ 35K\n- RSSM fidelity gap: obs MSE ratio and reward MAE ratio between dt=1 and dt=2\n- dt_embedding: learned embedding vector conditioned on dt∈{1,2}, concatenated to RSSM state\n- C6: imagination restricted to dt=1, but training data still includes dt=2 transitions\n- Uncertainty-gated truncation: monitors RSSM prediction uncertainty, truncates dt>1 when uncertainty exceeds threshold (1-seed pilot only)\n- Environments: Walker Walk, Cheetah Run, Cartpole Swingup, Hopper Hop (all DMC)\n- 3 seeds per configuration, IQM with 95% CI following Agarwal et al. 2021\n\n### Full Experiment Coverage\nTables 1-14 cover baselines, RSSM fidelity, embedding analysis, trained/untrained/removed dt_emb across 4 environments, C6 mitigation, KL divergence analysis, actor entropy dynamics, uncertainty-gated pilot, and aggregate metrics.\n\n### Your Review Task\n\nEvaluate the following aspects thoroughly:\n\n1. **Novelty Assessment**\n   - Is identifying this failure mode genuinely novel? Value overestimation in MBRL is well-known (Janner 2019, Pan 2020). How much does this add?\n   - Is the nve diagnostic metric a meaningful methodological contribution?\n   - Is the C6 mitigation (\"just use dt=1 imagination\") trivially obvious in hindsight?\n   - Does \"diagnosing why something fails\" constitute a sufficient contribution for a top venue?\n\n2. **Related Work Completeness**\n   - Missing references? Consider: TD-MPC (Hansen et al. 2022), IRIS (Micheli et al. 2023), other Transformer-based world models, TWM, STORM, etc.\n   - Multi-step prediction error analysis in dynamics models — any prior work?\n   - Value overestimation diagnostics — any existing metrics similar to nve?\n   - Temporal difference learning at multiple scales — relevant work?\n\n3. **Positioning and Framing**\n   - Is this positioned correctly as a \"diagnostic analysis\" paper?\n   - Would it be better as a workshop paper or short paper?\n   - Does the scope (DreamerV3 only, DMC only) match the claims?\n   - The \"delusional critic\" terminology — appropriate use given Lu et al. 2018's \"non-delusional Q-learning\"?\n\n4. **Breadth of Impact**\n   - Who would benefit from reading this paper?\n   - Does it advance the field or just explain a negative result?\n   - How actionable are the findings beyond DreamerV3?\n\nProvide your independent assessment:\n- Summary of strengths (bullet points)\n- Summary of weaknesses (bullet points)\n- Questions for authors\n- Preliminary score (1-6) with confidence (1-5)\n- Short justification\n\nKeep your review under 800 words.","uuid":"e0a48667-31e3-45a2-9709-c402f3603ac4","session_id":"31787645-5970-4613-84a7-699e9017e33d"}
