, non-delusional Q-learning (Lu et al. 2018)\n\nTotal references: ~14 (including Agarwal et al. 2021 for IQM, Henderson et al. 2018, Nikishin et al. 2022)\n\n### Key Technical Details\n- nve(t) = v/e_exp(t) / v/e_baseline(t), threshold 1.5× at steps ≥ 35K\n- RSSM fidelity gap: obs MSE ratio and reward MAE ratio between dt=1 and dt=2\n- dt_embedding: learned embedding vector conditioned on dt∈{1,2}, concatenated to RSSM state\n- C6: imagination restricted to dt=1, but training data still includes dt=2 transitions\n- Uncertainty-gated truncation: monitors RSSM prediction uncertainty, truncates dt>1 when uncertainty exceeds threshold (1-seed pilot only)\n- Environments: Walker Walk, Cheetah Run, Cartpole Swingup, Hopper Hop (all DMC)\n- 3 seeds per configuration, IQM with 95% CI following Agarwal et al. 2021\n\n### Full Experiment Coverage\nTables 1-14 cover baselines, RSSM fidelity, embedding analysis, trained/untrained/removed dt_emb across 4 environments, C6 mitigation, KL divergence analysis, actor entropy dynamics, uncertainty-gated pilot, and aggregate metrics.\n\n### Your Review Task\n\nEvaluate the following aspects thoroughly:\n\n1. **Novelty Assessment**\n   - Is identifying this failure mode genuinely novel? Value overestimation in MBRL is well-known (Janner 2019, Pan 2020). How much does this add?\n   - Is the nve diagnostic metric a meaningful methodological contribution?\n   - Is the C6 mitigation (\"just use dt=1 imagination\") trivially obvious in hindsight?\n   - Does \"diagnosing why something fails\" constitute a sufficient contribution for a top venue?\n\n2. **Related Work Completeness**\n   - Missing references? Consider: TD-MPC (Hansen et al. 2022), IRIS (Micheli et al. 2023), other Transformer-based world models, TWM, STORM, etc.\n   - Multi-step prediction error analysis in dynamics models — any prior work?\n   - Value overestimation diagnostics — any existing metrics similar to nve?\n   - Temporal difference learning at multiple scales — relevant work?\n\n3. **Positioning and Framing**\n   - Is this positioned correctly as a \"diagnostic analysis\" paper?\n   - Would it be better as a workshop paper or short paper?\n   - Does the scope (DreamerV3 only, DMC only) match the claims?\n   - The \"delusional critic\" terminology — appropriate use given Lu et al. 2018's \"non-delusional Q-learning\"?\n\n4. **Breadth of Impact**\n   - Who would benefit from reading this paper?\n   - Does it advance the field or just explain a negative result?\n   - How actionable are the findings beyond DreamerV3?\n\nProvide your independent assessment:\n- Summary of strengths (bullet points)\n- Summary of weaknesses (bullet points)\n- Questions for authors\n- Preliminary score (1-6) with confidence (1-5)\n- Short justification\n\nKeep your review under 800 words."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01ThN6WpRhxnFZ4u1h4UFPY2","session_id":"31787645-5970-4613-84a7-699e9017e33d","uuid":"40cb8517-fa05-4366-a3cb-48cbcc2a6dd2","timestamp":"2026-05-15T01:50:43.626Z"}
