{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01L4jssAZWLAQJYMSAJSFtZm","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Review submitted. Key findings:\n\n**Score: 3/6 (Weak Reject), Confidence: 3/5**\n\nThe review identifies seven substantive issues:\n\n1. **Data provenance** -- The most critical concern. Cross-referencing `imagined_experiments.yaml`, `decisions.yaml`, and `memory.md` reveals that only Walker Walk experiments have actually been run. Cheetah, Cartpole, and Hopper data are \"best-tier\" projections, not measurements. The paper's 18/18 classification accuracy and cross-environment claims rest on imagined data.\n\n2. **Post-hoc threshold** -- The nve>1.5x threshold was empirically selected from the same data used to evaluate it (D032 confirms this). No held-out validation or principled derivation is provided.\n\n3. **Single-environment mitigation** -- C6 validated only in Walker Walk despite architecture-level claims.\n\n4. **Confounded control** -- The dt_embed_dim=0 ablation simultaneously removes the hypothesized mechanism AND degrades reward prediction by 75x, preventing clean causal attribution.\n\n5. **No figures** -- A temporal-dynamics diagnostic paper with zero visualizations.\n\n6. **Marginal seed count** -- 3 seeds per config makes the 100% classification claim fragile (one miss = 94%).\n\n7. **Causal chain gap** -- \"Closed\" is overstated given the confounded ablation.\n\nThe review was saved to `/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_9/projects/event-gated-adaptive-horizon/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260515T004704/best/review_report.md`."},{"type":"text","text":"agentId: ab73c4ad517e43ec4 (use SendMessage with to: 'ab73c4ad517e43ec4' to continue this agent)\n<usage>total_tokens: 77016\ntool_uses: 13\nduration_ms: 120836</usage>"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"31787645-5970-4613-84a7-699e9017e33d","uuid":"c3dbaa39-1a8f-4af8-87a6-3d98d850d1ce","timestamp":"2026-05-15T01:52:18.663Z","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"You are Reviewer R1 for a top ML venue review (acceptance rate ~25%, 6-point scale: 1=Strong Reject, 2=Reject, 3=Weak Reject, 4=Weak Accept, 5=Accept, 6=Strong Accept).\n\nYour focus: **Methods and Experiments**.\n\n## Paper: \"Why Temporal Abstraction Fails in DreamerV3: A Diagnostic Analysis of Variable-Rate Imagination\"\n\n### Paper Summary\nThe paper diagnoses why variable-rate imagination fails in DreamerV3. The central claim is a closed causal chain: trained duration embeddings (dt_emb) exploit the RSSM's fidelity gap at dt>1, producing systematic value overestimation (\"delusional critic\"). They introduce \"normalized value-eval ratio\" (nve) as a diagnostic marker, achieving 18/18=100% classification accuracy across Walker Walk, Cheetah Run, and Cartpole Swingup (3 seeds each). A \"C6\" mitigation (restrict imagination to dt=1 while retaining multi-dt training) recovers 94.8% baseline in Walker Walk (3-seed IQM=870, CI [852,888]). An uncertainty-gated truncation pilot achieves 89% baseline.\n\n### Key Tables and Data\n\n**Table 1 - Baselines (dt=1, 500K steps, 3 seeds each):**\n- Walker Walk: IQM=947 [935,959]\n- Cheetah Run: IQM=783 [770,796]\n- Cartpole Swingup: IQM=843 [835,851]\n- Hopper Hop: IQM=305 [280,330]\n\n**Table 2 - RSSM Fidelity Gap (obs gap = MSE_dt2/MSE_dt1, reward gap = MAE_dt2/MAE_dt1):**\n- Walker baseline: obs 2.04×, reward 1.56×\n- Walker trained dt_emb: obs 1.30×, reward 2.78×\n- Walker no dt_emb: obs 2.75×, reward 1.01×\n- Cheetah trained: obs 1.35×, reward 2.55×\n- Cheetah no dt_emb: obs 2.80×, reward 1.03×\n- Cartpole trained: obs 1.28×, reward 2.40×\n- Pearson r between reward gap and nve = 0.87\n\n**Table 3 - dt embedding cosine similarity evolution:** 0.85→0.45→0.25→0.20 at 5K/25K/45K/105K. Norm ratio dt2/dt1: 1.02→1.20→1.30→1.35.\n\n**Table 4 - Walker trained dt_emb (3 seeds):**\n- Seed 0 (008d): nve 2.09×@45K, sustained, COLLAPSE (eval 83@55K)\n- Seed 1 (009e): nve 2.25×@45K, sustained, COLLAPSE (eval 72@55K)\n- Seed 2 (009b): nve 1.62×@45K, transient, NO collapse (eval 268@105K)\n\n**Table 5 - Cheetah trained dt_emb (3 seeds):** All exceed nve>1.5×, 1/3 collapse.\n\n**Table 6 - Cartpole trained dt_emb (3 seeds):** All exceed nve>1.5×, 1/3 collapse. Peaks: 2.10×, 1.55×, 1.52×.\n\n**Table 7 - Causal control (dt_emb removed):** 0/9 exceed nve>1.5× across Walker/Cheetah/Cartpole. Combined with 9/9 trained → 18/18=100% classification.\n\n**Table 8 - Untrained dt_emb:** Walker IQM=733 (80% baseline), Cheetah IQM=442 (75% baseline). nve consistently <1.0×.\n\n**Table 9 - C6 mitigation (Walker Walk):** Seeds: 869.9/858/882 → IQM=870, CI=[852,888], 94.8% baseline. nve 0.78-0.83×.\n\n**Table 10 - Classification accuracy:** 18/18 (100%) for 3 primary envs, 23/24 (96%) including Hopper.\n\n**Table 11 - KL divergence:** Baseline 0.08, Trained dt_emb 0.45, Untrained 0.12.\n\n**Table 12 - Hopper Hop:** Trained 2/3 exceed nve>1.5×, 1/3 collapse. No dt_emb 0/3 exceed. Classification 5/6 (83%).\n\n**Table 13 - Mitigation comparison (Walker):** Baseline 916, C6 870, Uncertainty-gated 815, No mitigation 83.\n\n**Table 14 - Key metrics vs targets:** All 6 metrics within target ranges.\n\n### Experiment Design Reference (from review context YAML)\nThe imagined experiment plan includes:\n- Walker Walk: baseline (3 seeds), trained dt_emb (3 seeds), no dt_emb (3 seeds), untrained dt_emb (3 seeds), C6 mitigation (3 seeds)\n- Cheetah Run: baseline (3 seeds), trained dt_emb (3 seeds), no dt_emb (3 seeds), untrained dt_emb (3 seeds)\n- Cartpole Swingup: baseline (3 seeds), trained dt_emb (3 seeds), no dt_emb (3 seeds)\n- Hopper Hop: baseline + trained + no dt_emb (3 seeds × 3 configs)\n- RSSM prediction quality analysis across envs\n- Actor entropy analysis\n- Value prediction distributional analysis (V(s) vs MC return)\n- dt_embedding cosine similarity analysis\n- Uncertainty-gated imagination truncation pilot (1 seed Walker)\n- Total ~160 GPU hours\n\n### Your Review Task\n\nEvaluate the following aspects thoroughly and provide:\n\n1. **Experimental Design Quality** (Are the factorial design, controls, and ablations well-structured? Are there confounds?)\n2. **Statistical Rigor** (3 seeds adequate? CI methodology? Is IQM appropriate? How robust are the 100% classification claims?)\n3. **Causal Claims** (Is the \"closed causal chain\" actually established? Are there alternative explanations?)\n4. **Metric Design** (Is nve well-motivated? Is the 1.5× threshold principled or post-hoc?)\n5. **Completeness of Experiments** (Are key experiments missing? Cross-env C6 validation? More environments/architectures?)\n6. **Reproducibility** (Enough implementation detail? Hyperparameters reported?)\n7. **Figures and Presentation** (The paper has only tables, no figures — is this a problem?)\n\nProvide your independent assessment:\n- Summary of strengths (bullet points)\n- Summary of weaknesses (bullet points)  \n- Questions for authors\n- Preliminary score (1-6) with confidence (1-5)\n- Short justification\n\nKeep your review under 800 words.","agentId":"ab73c4ad517e43ec4","agentType":"general-purpose","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Review submitted. Key findings:\n\n**Score: 3/6 (Weak Reject), Confidence: 3/5**\n\nThe review identifies seven substantive issues:\n\n1. **Data provenance** -- The most critical concern. Cross-referencing `imagined_experiments.yaml`, `decisions.yaml`, and `memory.md` reveals that only Walker Walk experiments have actually been run. Cheetah, Cartpole, and Hopper data are \"best-tier\" projections, not measurements. The paper's 18/18 classification accuracy and cross-environment claims rest on imagined data.\n\n2. **Post-hoc threshold** -- The nve>1.5x threshold was empirically selected from the same data used to evaluate it (D032 confirms this). No held-out validation or principled derivation is provided.\n\n3. **Single-environment mitigation** -- C6 validated only in Walker Walk despite architecture-level claims.\n\n4. **Confounded control** -- The dt_embed_dim=0 ablation simultaneously removes the hypothesized mechanism AND degrades reward prediction by 75x, preventing clean causal attribution.\n\n5. **No figures** -- A temporal-dynamics diagnostic paper with zero visualizations.\n\n6. **Marginal seed count** -- 3 seeds per config makes the 100% classification claim fragile (one miss = 94%).\n\n7. **Causal chain gap** -- \"Closed\" is overstated given the confounded ablation.\n\nThe review was saved to `/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_9/projects/event-gated-adaptive-horizon/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260515T004704/best/review_report.md`."}],"totalDurationMs":120836,"totalTokens":77016,"totalToolUseCount":13,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3772,"cache_read_input_tokens":72847,"output_tokens":396,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3772},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":396,"cache_read_input_tokens":72847,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3772,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3772,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"toolStats":{"readCount":3,"searchCount":2,"bashCount":0,"editFileCount":0,"linesAdded":0,"linesRemoved":0,"otherToolCount":8}}}
